# Conventional Commits

When the user asks you to **create a git commit** or **open a pull request**, format the message/title using [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/).

Do not use this format for casual chat replies — only for git commit messages and PR titles/bodies when committing or creating PRs is part of the task.

## Format

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <short summary>

<optional body>

<optional footer>
```

- Summary: imperative mood, lower case, no trailing period, <= 72 chars.
- Leave a blank line before the body and before any footer.
- Use the body to explain the **why**, not a file list.

## Allowed types

- `feat` — new feature or player-facing behavior
- `fix` — bug fix (including build/runtime crashes)
- `docs` — documentation only (README, `.cursor/plan/`, comments in docs)
- `style` — formatting or visual-only changes with no logic change
- `refactor` — code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
- `perf` — performance improvement
- `test` — adding or fixing tests
- `chore` — tooling, config, or maintenance
- `build` / `ci` — build settings, pipelines, player builds

## Scope (this project)

Optional, lower case. Prefer scopes that match areas in this repo:

- `playtest` — Start/GameOver flow, run timing, build-scene tools
- `ui` — scene controllers, HUD, menus
- `scenes` — `.unity` scene or build-settings changes
- `editor` — `Assets/WhoWiredThis/Editor/` tools and validators
- `puzzle` — puzzle managers, transitions, tutorial/puzzle scenes
- `prefab` — prefab or variant changes
- `config` — ProjectSettings, packages, render/input settings
- `docs` — plan archive, README, cursor rules

## Breaking changes

Add `!` after the type/scope and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.

## Examples (Who Wired This)

```
feat(playtest): add start and game over scene flow with summed run time
fix(playtest): repair broken Room5x5 serialization that crashed player loads
fix(editor): pass OK button to DisplayDialog in build scene validator
docs(playtest): archive plan for start gameover total time flow
chore(editor): add MCP menu items for playtest validate and repair
build(scenes): enable playtest scenes in editor build settings
refactor(ui): load scenes via PlaytestSceneLoadUtility before BeginRun
```

## With the user's git commit workflow

When committing on request, still follow the user's git safety steps (status, diff, log style). **Draft the commit message in Conventional Commits format** before running `git commit`.

## Git push (not automatic)

- **Do not push** to the remote unless the user explicitly asks (e.g. "push", "push to origin").
- Creating a commit does **not** imply permission to push.
- After a successful local commit, stop unless the user requested push or a PR (PR creation may require push only when the user asked for the PR and the branch is not on the remote yet).
